s to  do it i don't know if like  most modern shows don't have the balls  to like drop all the characters and then  start over with new characters after a  few episodes most shows would not do  that so it remains to be seen the  trailer itself looks so high quality  that's one thing that i've said that  really excited me about the first  trailer like the high qualitiness of it  high qualitiness i don't know if that's  actual english but it looks really  really good the cgi looks really really  good the sets look really good the  costumes look really good it's very very  very high budget that of course isn't  everything but what it does show is that  there is a lot of investment behind this  show it does not look cheap it does not  look like something that was just kind  of slapped together and one thing that i  noticed about the trailer too is that  this one's really  kind of focusing in on harry selden as  kind of the shepherd of humanity's  future there's even a part in the  trailer where you see him caress a  younger character's face almost like a  father figure  which is interesting because you know in  those foundation books harry seldon does  kind of act like a father to the  foundation he like is the only character  that shows up again and again and again  because he's been preserved in  holographic recordings that um appear at  certain times not without spoiling too  much but it also looks like from looking  at the trailer that these characters are  also given giving emphasized roles it  looks like there's new characters like  this triple emperor person  um is not from the book i'm not sure  what's going on with that so it looks  like they're setting up some new things  because it is a tv show and for a modern  tv show you do have to like the  characters have to be real and they have  to be people and we have to be able to  relate with characters to keep people  engaged with the modern tv show as  opposed to the book which really is just  about the formation